A||N||2||mrossum||head lamp motors||||1||
Z||000000||mrossum||08-05-2001||11:34 PM||||tried to put a pair of 84-6 style head lamp motors on a 87 car. turned the lights on, and they went up, but when lights turned off, they stayed up. any ideas?????||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-06-2001||12:39 AM||||1987-later cars have an electronic controller that runs the headlight motors.  They use a completely different motor design.  For example, the 1987-later motors have two terminals, while the 1984-1986 motors have three terminals.<P>Your best bet is to just get a pair of 1987-later headlight motors, the ones that were meant to work with the electronic controller.<P>It <B>is</B> possible to modify the 1984-1986 motors to work with the electronic system.  I did it kind of as an experiment.  But it isn't too easy, and it really wasn't worth it, in retrospect.  The 1987-later motors work better and faster than the earlier relay-operated ones, are more reliable and easier to rebuild.     <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000002||JohnA||08-07-2001||09:29 AM||||You can find a great deal of info on this matter at the Fiero Virtual repair shop. Helped me. Good Luck<BR> <A HREF="http://www.members.tripod.com/FieroDough/localrepair.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.tripod.com/FieroDough/localrepair.htm</A> ||||reg||14
